 class _InternalURLCache(TypedDict, total=False):
+    """Per-instance cache for lazily computed or expensive-to-parse values.
+
+    Cache lifecycle
+    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+    - **Creation**: Every constructor sets ``self._cache = {}`` (a fresh,
+      instance-owned dict).  The dict is never shared between URL objects.
+    - **Write-once population**: Keys are added lazily when a property is
+      first accessed.  Once a key is present it is never invalidated,
+      because the underlying URL attributes are immutable.
+    - **Pickle / unpickle**: ``__setstate__`` calls ``_reset_cache()`` to
+      discard any cached values from the pickled instance.  This prevents
+      the unpickled object from sharing stale references with the original
+      and ensures that subsequent property accesses recompute against the
+      restored attributes.
+
+    Keys actually stored at runtime
+    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+    Only a subset of the keys below are ever written into the dict; the
+    rest exist here solely for static type checking of ``cached_property``
+    descriptors that conceptually belong to the same "cached" family.
+
+    - ``hash`` -- written by :meth:`__hash__` on first call.
+    - ``raw_user``, ``raw_password``, ``raw_host``, ``explicit_port`` --
+      written together by :meth:`_populate_netloc_cache` when any netloc sub-
+      component is first requested.
